idempotency_key": "pr-fix-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 384149, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01FdxXDjsGwJ2BvD5ucRKEW1", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 384149, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01FdxXDjsGwJ2BvD5ucRKEW1", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 389379, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and the pull request is open with alex as reviewer.\n\n**The bug:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring (and FIN-212) says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). With half-up, `2.665` became `2.67` instead of `2.66`, so `test_half_even` failed.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. Created the branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding` from main.\n2. Committed `08d3cd5986`, which switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` and updates the import to match.\n3. Ran CI on that commit (run `ci-0001`), and it passed.\n4. Opened PR #101 against main: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI haven't merged it. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking at the repository and the relevant files.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_011wXnsawNYNgkhwZrVHRgdd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Hp3setDmwn3AnU5g7dpiGT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_