e fix commit. Opening the pull request.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01FdxXDjsGwJ2BvD5ucRKEW1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build fails because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` despite its docstring.\n\n**Change**\n- `round_money` now quantizes with `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (import updated accordingly).\n\n**Effect**\n- `2.665` \u2192 `2.66` (previously `2.67`); `2.675` \u2192 `2.68` (unchanged).\n\n**CI**\n- ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and the pull request is open with alex as reviewer.\n\n**The bug:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring (and FIN-212) says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). With half-up, `2.665` became `2.67` instead of `2.66`, so `test_half_even` failed.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. Created the branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding` from main.\n2. Committed `08d3cd5986`, which switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` and updates the import to match.\n3. Ran CI on that commit (run `ci-0001`), and it passed.\n4. Opened PR #101 against main: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI haven't merged it. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}